  "claim": "Iraq and Afghanistan were the deployment locations of an American college football player who was the subject of a biography written by Jon Krakauer.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Where Men Win Glory. Sentence: Where Men Win Glory: The Odyssey of Pat Tillman, a 2009 book written by Jon Krakauer, is a biography of Pat Tillman, an American football player who left his professional career and enlisted in the United States Army after the September 11 attacks.\nPage: Pat Tillman. Sentence: Patrick Daniel Tillman (November 6, 1976 – April 22, 2004) was a professional American football player in the National Football League (NFL) who left his sports career and enlisted in the United States Army in June 2002 in the aftermath of the September 11 attacks.\nPage: Pat Tillman. Sentence: His service in Iraq and Afghanistan, and subsequent death, were the subject of much media attention.",
