        "original_id": "49188093-c407-5d0b-abd8-8591f9a1d219",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pat Tillman, Jon Krakauer\n- Products: Where Men Win Glory: The Odyssey of Pat Tillman\n- Organizations: United States Army, National Football League\n- Events: September 11 attacks\n- Topics: military service, media attention, death\n\nFacts:\n- Pat Tillman was born on November 6, 1976.\n- Pat Tillman was a professional American football player in the National Football League.\n- In the aftermath of the September 11 attacks, Pat Tillman left his professional football career and enlisted in the United States Army in June 2002.\n- Pat Tillman served in Iraq and Afghanistan.\n- Pat Tillman died on April 22, 2004.\n- Pat Tillman’s service in Iraq and Afghanistan and his death received extensive media attention.\n- Jon Krakauer wrote Where Men Win Glory: The Odyssey of Pat Tillman in 2009.\n- Where Men Win Glory: The Odyssey of Pat Tillman is a biography of Pat Tillman.",
